{"name":"Tory Red","hex":"#d6685f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Tory."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Tory."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tory"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tory","blocks":[{"text":"A Tory is an individual who supports a political philosophy known as Toryism, based on a British version of traditionalist conservatism which upholds the established social order as it has evolved through the history of Great Britain. The Tory ethos has been summed up with the phrase \"God, King and Country\". Tories are monarchists, were historically of a high church Anglican religious heritage, and were opposed to the liberalism of the Whig party."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tory"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Royal_Oak.png/500px-Royal_Oak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Royal_Oak.png/500px-Royal_Oak.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoyal_Oak.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg/500px-Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg/1280px-Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg/500px-Anthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Royalist supporters, such as the Cavaliers, were referred to as tories during the Interregnum and Restoration period in Great Britain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnthonis_van_Dyck_058.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg/500px-John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg/1280px-John_Belasyse_%28Bellasis%29%2C_1st_Baron_Belasyse_of_Worlaby_by_Gilbert_Jackson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp